
$ Validation: Cantilever with transverse-offset tip mass — coupled
$ bending-torsion modes (SOL 103)
$
$ Purpose:   Demonstrates the CONM2 offset coupling: a tip mass whose CG sits
$            off the elastic axis (offset d in +Y) couples Z-bending (Tz) with
$            torsion (Rx) through the full 6x6 CONM2 mass block — the m*[r]x
$            translation-rotation coupling and the parallel-axis term m*d^2.
$            Without the offset, bending and torsion are independent mode
$            families; with it, both modes below carry twist AND deflection.
$
$ Geometry:  L = 10 m, 10 equal CBAR elements (1 m each), 11 nodes along X
$ Material:  Steel — E = 200 GPa, G = 76.92 GPa, nu = 0.3, rho = 7850 kg/m^3
$ Section:   Solid square, side a = 0.1 m
$              A  = 0.01 m^2
$              I1 = I2 = a^4/12  = 8.3333e-6 m^4
$              J  = 0.1406*a^4   = 1.406e-5  m^4
$ Tip mass:  CONM2 m = 5000 kg at node 11, offset (0, 1.5, 0) m,
$            I11 = 5000 kg.m^2 (pod inertia about its own CG, X-axis)
$ BCs:       Encastre at node 1. DOFs 1,2,6 (Tx, Ty, Rz) fixed at nodes 2-11
$            so the axial and XY-bending families are suppressed and the
$            deck isolates the coupled Z-bending/torsion family (Tz, Rx, Ry).
$
$ Closed form (tip-dominant 2-DOF, Rayleigh corrections for beam mass):
$   k_w     = 3EI/L^3                    = 5000.0   N/m
$   k_theta = GJ/L                       = 1.0815e5 N.m/rad
$   m_eff   = m + (33/140)*rho*A*L       = 5185.0   kg
$   I_eff   = m*d^2 + I11 + rho*Ip*L/3   = 16250.4  kg.m^2   (Ip = I1+I2)
$   M = [[m_eff, m*d], [m*d, I_eff]],  K = diag(k_w, k_theta)
$   det(K - w^2 M) = 0  ->  f1 = 0.14895 Hz   (bending-dominant, ~10% twist)
$                           f2 = 0.74728 Hz   (torsion-dominant)
$
$ Expected (this deck, consistent-mass FE):
$   f1 ~= 0.1489 Hz   coupled mode 1 — bending-dominant, tip Rx*d/Tz ~ +0.10
$   f2 ~= 0.7466 Hz   coupled mode 2 — torsion-dominant, tip Rx*d/Tz ~ -0.99
$   f3 ~= 3.68 Hz, f4 ~= 11.7 Hz — continuum beam modes (tip nearly a node)
$   Setting the CONM2 offset X2 = 0.0 decouples the families: mode 1 becomes
$   pure bending sqrt(k_w/m_eff)/2pi ~= 0.156 Hz and the torsion mode becomes
$   pure sqrt(k_theta/(I11 + rho*Ip*L/3))/2pi ~= 0.740 Hz.
$ Units:     SI (m, N, kg, Pa)
$
SOL 103
$
SUBCASE 1
  TITLE  = Offset Tip Mass — Coupled Bending-Torsion Modes
  SPC    = 1
  METHOD = 20
$
BEGIN BULK
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------ NODES
$ GRID, GID, CP, X1,  X2,  X3, CD, PS, SEID
GRID,  1, , 0.0,  0.0, 0.0
GRID,  2, , 1.0,  0.0, 0.0
GRID,  3, , 2.0,  0.0, 0.0
GRID,  4, , 3.0,  0.0, 0.0
GRID,  5, , 4.0,  0.0, 0.0
GRID,  6, , 5.0,  0.0, 0.0
GRID,  7, , 6.0,  0.0, 0.0
GRID,  8, , 7.0,  0.0, 0.0
GRID,  9, , 8.0,  0.0, 0.0
GRID, 10, , 9.0,  0.0, 0.0
GRID, 11, , 10.0, 0.0, 0.0
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------------- MATERIAL
$ MAT1, MID, E,      G,        NU,  RHO
MAT1, 1, 2.0e11, 7.692e10, 0.3, 7850.0
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------- PROPERTIES
$ PBAR, PID, MID, A,    I1,        I2,        J
$ Solid square, a = 0.1 m
PBAR, 1, 1, 0.01, 8.3333e-6, 8.3333e-6, 1.406e-5
$ +,   C1,    C2,    D1,     D2,    E1,     E2,     F1,    F2
+,    0.05,  0.05, -0.05,   0.05, -0.05,  -0.05,   0.05, -0.05
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------------- ELEMENTS
$ CBAR, EID, PID, GA, GB, X1,  X2,  X3
$ Orientation vector (0,1,0): local y = global Y
CBAR,  1, 1,  1,  2, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR,  2, 1,  2,  3, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR,  3, 1,  3,  4, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR,  4, 1,  4,  5, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR,  5, 1,  5,  6, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR,  6, 1,  6,  7, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR,  7, 1,  7,  8, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR,  8, 1,  8,  9, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR,  9, 1,  9, 10, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
CBAR, 10, 1, 10, 11, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------- TIP MASS (CONM2)
$ CONM2, EID, GID, CID, M,      X1,  X2,  X3,  I11
$ 5000 kg pod, CG offset 1.5 m in +Y off the elastic axis,
$ I11 = 5000 kg.m^2 about its own CG. The offset generates the
$ translation-rotation coupling and the m*d^2 parallel-axis inertia.
CONM2, 1, 11, 0, 5000.0, 0.0, 1.5, 0.0, 5000.0
$
$ ----------------------------------------------------------- CONSTRAINTS
$ SPC1, SID, C, G
$ Encastre at node 1 — all 6 DOFs fixed
SPC1, 1, 123456, 1
$ Suppress axial (Tx) and XY-bending (Ty, Rz) families at nodes 2-11:
$ the model retains the Tz / Rx / Ry family — Z-bending + torsion only
SPC1, 1, 126, 11, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2
$
$ --------------------------------------------------------- EIGENVALUE METHOD
$ EIGRL, SID, V1, V2, ND, MSGLVL, MAXSET, SHFSCL, NORM
$ Extract first 4 modes, MASS normalisation
EIGRL, 20, , , 4, , , , MASS
$
ENDDATA
